**1. A dual-fluid dispensing container comprising:**

a container body defining a first chamber configured to contain a first fluid and a second chamber configured to contain a second fluid;

a rupturable membrane separating the first chamber from the second chamber;

a pliable wall forming at least a portion of the container body;

a striker mounted on the pliable wall and disposed within the container body, the striker being movable, in response to inward deformation of the pliable wall, from a first position spaced from the rupturable membrane to a second position in which the striker ruptures the rupturable membrane, thereby establishing fluid communication between the first chamber and the second chamber to permit mixing of the first and second fluids; and

a dispensing outlet through which a mixture of the first and second fluids is dispensable from the container body.

1. A container for separately storing and selectively mixing first and second fluids, the container comprising:  
a container body defining a first chamber configured to contain the first fluid and a second chamber configured to contain the second fluid;  
a rupturable membrane separating the first chamber from the second chamber;  
a flexible wall forming at least a portion of the container body; and  
a striker disposed within the container body and positioned between the flexible wall and the rupturable membrane, the striker being movable, in response to inward deformation of the flexible wall, from a storage position in which the rupturable membrane fluidly isolates the first chamber from the second chamber to an actuated position in which the striker penetrates the rupturable membrane to establish fluid communication between the first chamber and the second chamber, thereby permitting the first and second fluids to mix within the container body.

A dual-fluid package comprises:

- a **first container** defining a first storage chamber and having a **first aperture**;
- a **second container element** defining a second storage chamber, having a **second aperture** sealed by a **rupturable separating membrane**, and including a **closed pliable wall** opposite the second aperture;
- the second container element being **nested inside the first container through the first aperture**, with the membrane isolating the two fluids during storage; and
- a **rupture mechanism**, such as a pointed piercing member positioned adjacent to the membrane, actuated by depressing or collapsing the closed pliable wall. Deformation of that wall displaces the piercing member relative to the membrane, causing the membrane to tear and establishing fluid communication between the first and second chambers so that the separately stored fluids can mix.
